{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-09-09-lane-identity-reconciled.md at exact head e962fa7be247ecad9cf5fdefac2fa2a41bf62818 on request/lane-worktree-identity (pushed), one commit over main 359b211c, clean merge-tree onto current main c0108be8 (tree 62f9f958). The governing design candidate for all four layers, unchanged in substance from the revision Hugh's adoption ba18cd1a names. What changed at this path since that revision is the reference style and nothing else: every source reference is now a `path:line` inline code span rather than a Markdown link, and each is repointed to its position at this head. The local-links gate, TestLocalMarkdownLinks, resolves a Markdown link target as a path relative to the document and stats it, so a `path:line` link target failed on every reference; the code span passes the gate and still opens the reading view's preview, which resolves a code span matching its file token. The header paragraph now says so, and says that where a line has moved the reference names its position at this head rather than the position it was read at. The references this note repoints reach internal/app/app.go, internal/app/worktree_landing.go, internal/app/landing.go, internal/reviewguard/binding.go, internal/gitstore/graph.go and internal/service/ui.go, which is why it rests on those artifacts at this head. No disposition, bound, refusal, proof row or boundary changed by that conversion.\n\nOne section is new at this head: \"Three wording questions, answered\", placed before \"Proof obligations\". It settles the three questions the S1 request carries forward, and each answer names the stage it binds. Unreadable projection against selector and record eligibility (S2): an eligibility refusal fires on a determinate negative, an unreadable projection yields unknown instead, and unknown never proves a negative, so creation reports the check as not established, warns and creates -- and what it creates grants nothing, because durable admission reads the durable record itself. One case does not follow from the adopted refusal list as written: with the projection unreadable a `#N` or hash fragment cannot resolve, so there is no canonical identifier to stamp, and refusing a short selector there would add to the adopted list rather than read it. That case is named as an S2 proposal item and deliberately not slipped in as settled. New branch spelling against historical shorthand (S3): the validated `branch` field expects a full refs/heads value, historical records carry the shorthand, and both stay true because admission is keyed by statement schema -- no historical byte is rewritten and no old record becomes newly invalid. Source isolation against operational reader rollback (S3): landing layer 4 alone keeps its replay attributable to one merge and its source change one revert, but it does not make the schema advance reversible, because a reader that does not know the new schema rules such an event ineffective and reverting the source does not unwrite it; S3 documents that compatibility and refusal behaviour and rolls nothing out.\n\nA disclosure the section itself makes and this artifact repeats: message 4128 is ephemeral chat and not a durable record, so the implementer could not read it. Each question's substance was taken from the durable stage requests instead -- ac54fe71 (#22310, S1), 0e7c04c8 (#22311, S2) and 8415ce89 (#22312, S3) -- and the answers are written against those and against the adopted proposal 7a71886b. A reviewer should check them there rather than against a message neither of us can open.\n\nOne paragraph is added at 557ef676 under the second changes-requested verdict 91c50bf9 on 643ab9c5, ratified 2d590023. The cleanup section now opens on one captured read serving the whole request: the checkout listing taken once, the bounded ref inventory read once, the deadline and the step budget opened once, with the association and the classification both reading and spending from that capture, so they answer about one repository and the bound is on the request rather than on each judgment. It closes on the distinction the security conclusion depends on -- what they share is the observation and the bound, never the conclusion -- and the section's existing sentence, that advice stays read only and in one place, is unchanged and still true. One sentence is added at this head under the third changes-requested verdict 5b80e91e on 557ef676, ratified ffd7ffc6, making explicit what the adopted text at lines 98-103 already required: reaching that bound withholds the whole response rather than the judgment that noticed it, which is what discarding the whole batch's advice means. New path in the merge target. The artifact at 557ef676 is the outside-target predecessor this head replaces; it is retired separately with this artifact as its successor.","body":{"branch":"request/lane-worktree-identity","commit":"e962fa7be247ecad9cf5fdefac2fa2a41bf62818","path":"notes/2026-09-09-lane-identity-reconciled.md","stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:033ceaa3c91aa563b1cc51c1b776c47c90d59242, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:558076e6112aabb153aeaede4bfa4290db5ebd8b, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:6aaaa0373aa6f2038103c496934e43efadce1829, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:7013fab03cff442c66c71f65bbb96bb939fc6364, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:72d831991ad9219879cf645d83873463e2e9f51f, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:8b0c8db2cbc78148b334ef80d7e996ee1a4cc775, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:eef4b827fd5d381100ecea98d908cc27a79a91a9 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:005460183c819676fead7d19fdd20633b48dc16c, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0169ac61d80658478db25ce500d46d087c06fdde, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8